userStories.notes:
MIDDLEWARE PLACEMENT: Swagger middleware must go BETWEEN app.UseCors("FrontendPolicy") and app.UseAuthentication() in the pipeline. Do NOT place it before UseCors (CORS headers would be missing on Swagger responses) and not after UseAuthentication (would cause auth challenges on swagger.json requests). The exact insertion point in the current pipeline:
  app.UseCors("FrontendPolicy");
  [INSERT: if (app.Environment.IsDevelopment() || ...) { UseSwagger(); UseSwaggerUI(); }]
  app.UseAuthentication();
  app.UseAuthorization();
  app.MapControllers();

DEVELOPMENT ENV: Docker Compose already sets ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development via environment section — no additional config needed. The IsDevelopment() check will be true when running via docker compose up.

XML FILE GUARD: The XML doc file is only generated after a successful build. Add a File.Exists guard before calling IncludeXmlComments to avoid a startup crash on clean checkouts. Pattern: var xmlPath = Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "DevolveFacill.Api.xml"); if (File.Exists(xmlPath)) opt.IncludeXmlComments(xmlPath, includeControllerXmlComments: true);

Note: US-003 must be complete first so controllers have [ApiVersion] attributes and Swashbuckle can correctly group them under v1.
